  "limitations": [
    "2-D planar model: end effects and the real 3-D turn geometry are ignored; energies per unit depth are scaled by MLT/2 (leakage) and the core depth (magnetising).",
    "Winding blocks carry uniform current density (stranded assumption) in the magnetostatic solves.",
    "The 100 kHz AC loss factor uses a HOMOGENISED solid-block conductivity (sigma_eff = fill * sigma_cu); each block carries its total N*I (enforced by superposing unit-source solves) but current may redistribute freely inside the block as in a single massive conductor. It is an approximation indicator (close to a one-turn foil of the block width), not a Litz or multi-turn foil winding loss prediction.",
    "The Litz proximity estimate assumes strand diameter << skin depth and uses the magnetostatic field (no field redistribution).",
    "No measured validation; core modelled as linear, lossless, mu_r constant."
  ],
